@startuml campusclaw_invocation_logging_architecture
title CampusClaw Backend Logging and Diagnostics Architecture

' Source evidence:
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/CampusClawApplication.java:29-33, main
' mate-campusclaw/src/main/resources/application.properties:35-53, mirror startup configuration
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java:61-77, submit
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeExceptionHandler.java:45-67, handlers
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java:156-217, completeExecution and logFailure
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/mate/MateServiceModelManagerProvider.java:105-156, streamSimple and decodeResponse
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/application.yml:110-114, WARN logging baseline
' Observed behavior: there is no common ingress access log, provider failures can become terminal error messages without a Throwable, and the final execution logger only logs a non-null Throwable.
' Architecture change: add structured lifecycle events, an immutable diagnostic context, and explicit terminal outcome logging across servlet, virtual-thread, and Reactor boundaries.
' Design reason: operators must distinguish calls that never reached CampusClaw from request rejection, accepted execution failure, downstream model failure, and client disconnect.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #475569
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #475569
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

actor "Process Launcher" as Launcher
actor "mate-service\nor internal SDK" as Caller

rectangle "CampusClaw Startup Boundary" {
  component "Startup Lifecycle\nstart, ready, failure, shutdown" as Startup
  component "Required Startup Checks\ndatabase, schema, agent cache root" as StartupChecks
}

database "GaussDB Session Schema" as Database
folder "Agent Cache Root" as AgentCache

rectangle "Caller Boundary" {
  component "CampusClaw Client\nTarget-only in mate-service" as Client
  component "Client Invocation Logger\ncaller-side transport outcome" as ClientLog
}

cloud "Gateway and Network" as Network

rectangle "CampusClaw HTTP Boundary" {
  component "Request Logging Filter\nrequest start and completion" as Filter
  component "Runtime Controllers and Advice\noperation and result code" as Web
  component "SSE Delivery Observer\ndisconnect and terminal outcome" as SseObserver
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Execution Boundary" {
  component "RuntimeEventService\naccept user entry" as EventService
  component "Immutable InvocationLogContext\nrequest, session, execution" as Context
  component "RuntimeExecutionCoordinator\nauthoritative terminal outcome" as Coordinator
  component "Agent and Tool Pipeline" as Agent
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Model Boundary" {
  component "MateServiceModelManagerProvider" as Provider
  component "Mate Chat SSE Parser\nstable failure stage and code" as Parser
}

rectangle "Logging Output" {
  component "SLF4J Key-Value Events" as Slf4j
  component "Spring Boot ECS Encoder" as Ecs
  queue "Container stdout" as Stdout
  component "Platform Collector and Search" as Collector
}

rectangle "CampusMate Model Manager" {
  component "POST /mate-service/v1/LLM/chat" as ModelManager
}

Caller --> Client
Launcher --> Startup : launch process
Startup --> StartupChecks : run before ready
StartupChecks --> Database : connect and read-only schema probe
StartupChecks --> AgentCache : safe write and delete probe
Client --> ClientLog : start and completion
Client --> Network : HTTP or HTTP plus SSE
Network --> Filter
Filter --> Web
Web --> EventService
EventService --> Context : create and enrich
EventService --> Coordinator
Coordinator --> Agent
Agent --> Provider
Provider --> ModelManager
ModelManager --> Parser : HTTP and SSE outcome
Parser --> Provider
Coordinator --> SseObserver

Filter --> Slf4j
Startup --> Slf4j
StartupChecks --> Slf4j
Web --> Slf4j
SseObserver --> Slf4j
Coordinator --> Slf4j
Provider --> Slf4j
ClientLog --> Slf4j
Slf4j --> Ecs
Ecs --> Stdout
Stdout --> Collector

note bottom of Context
MDC is not the source of truth after request-thread exit.
The immutable context is passed explicitly to execution and model calls.
end note

note bottom of ClientLog
If connect or routing fails before CampusClaw,
only the caller can produce the failure log.
end note

note bottom of Slf4j
No credentials, headers, prompts, message bodies,
thinking, tool arguments, tool results, or raw SSE.
end note

note bottom of StartupChecks
startup.completed is emitted only after all required checks
and the web server binding have succeeded.
Remote model and tool services are lazy runtime dependencies.
end note
@enduml

@startuml campusclaw_failure_logging_sequence
title Failure Diagnosis Across the CampusClaw Call

' Source evidence:
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/mate/MateChatSseParser.java:80-133, accept, fail, and parseChunk
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java:100-107, terminal ERROR breaks without throwing
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java:223-240, persistAssistant
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeTerminalEventFactory.java:34-57, stream.error selection
' Observed behavior: a model error can reach stream.error while RuntimeExecutionCoordinator receives no Throwable and therefore writes no failure log.
' Architecture change: each boundary emits one start and one terminal event with a shared local diagnostic context and a stable failure stage.
' Design reason: the absence and order of events must identify the failing boundary without logging payloads.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #334155
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "mate-service" as Caller
participant "Caller Client Logger" as CallerLog
participant "Network" as Network
participant "Request Logging Filter" as Filter
participant "Runtime Event API" as Api
participant "Execution Coordinator" as Coordinator
participant "Mate Model Provider" as Provider
participant "Model Manager" as Manager
participant "Structured Log Sink" as Logs

Caller -> CallerLog : client.call.started
Caller -> Network : POST Session Events

alt Connection or routing fails before CampusClaw
  Network --> Caller : connect, TLS, DNS, or route failure
  CallerLog -> Logs : client.call.completed failure\nfailureStage=campusclaw_connect
  note over Filter
  No CampusClaw ingress event is expected.
  end note
else Request reaches CampusClaw
  Network -> Filter : HTTP request
  Filter -> Logs : http.request.started
  Filter -> Api : dispatch validated route

  alt Request rejected before SSE starts
    Api --> Filter : 4xx or 5xx with stable resCode
    Filter -> Logs : http.request.completed rejected or failed
    Filter --> Network : JSON error
    Network --> Caller : HTTP failure
    CallerLog -> Logs : client.call.completed failure
  else User entry is accepted
    Api -> Coordinator : start execution
    Coordinator -> Logs : execution.started
    Coordinator -> Provider : invoke model
    Provider -> Logs : model.invocation.started
    Provider -> Manager : POST Mate Chat

    alt Model HTTP, stream, or parser failure
      Manager --> Provider : non-2xx, error event, invalid SSE, or close
      Provider -> Logs : model.invocation.completed failure\nfailureStage and safe errorCode
      Provider --> Coordinator : terminal StopReason.ERROR
      Coordinator -> Logs : execution.completed failure\nerrorCode=SESSION_EXECUTION_FAILED
      Coordinator --> Api : stream.error then close
      Api -> Logs : sse.completed failure
      Api --> Network : HTTP 200 stream.error
      Network --> Caller : stream failure
      CallerLog -> Logs : client.call.completed failure
    else Client disconnects after acceptance
      Caller --> Network : close response body
      Network --> Api : write failure or async error
      Api -> Logs : sse.disconnected\nexecutionContinues=true
      Coordinator -> Manager : continue accepted execution
      Coordinator -> Logs : execution.completed success or failure
      CallerLog -> Logs : client.call.completed disconnected
    else Normal completion
      Manager --> Provider : valid chunks and DONE
      Provider -> Logs : model.invocation.completed success
      Provider --> Coordinator : terminal message
      Coordinator -> Logs : execution.completed success
      Coordinator --> Api : stream.end
      Api -> Logs : sse.completed success
      Api --> Network : close SSE
      Network --> Caller : normal completion
      CallerLog -> Logs : client.call.completed success
    end
  end
end
@enduml

@startuml campusclaw_startup_logging_sequence
title CampusClaw Backend Startup Diagnostics

' Source evidence:
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/CampusClawApplication.java:29-33, main
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/application.yml:9-34, datasource and server settings
' mate-campusclaw/src/main/resources/application.properties:35-53, mirror datasource and server settings
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/builtin/BuiltInToolProperties.java:90-107, startup validation
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/mate/MateServiceModelManagerProvider.java:68-92, provider configuration validation
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java:127-160, lazy cache-root creation
' Observed behavior: the application has no stable startup lifecycle event, the mirror disables Hikari initial failure, and schema plus cache-root readiness are not proven before the server reports ready.
' Architecture change: register a pre-context lifecycle listener and run database, schema, and cache-root checks before the web-server connector starts.
' Design reason: startup.completed must prove that the backend can accept and persist a basic Session request, while startup.failed must identify the failing stage without exposing configuration secrets.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #334155
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "Operator or Container" as Operator
participant "SpringApplication" as Spring
participant "Startup Lifecycle" as Lifecycle
participant "Application Context" as Context
participant "Web Server" as WebServer
participant "Startup Diagnostic Gate" as Gate
database "GaussDB" as Database
participant "Agent Cache Root" as CacheRoot
participant "Structured Log Sink" as Logs

Operator -> Spring : launch backend
Spring -> Lifecycle : environment prepared
Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.started
Spring -> Context : bind configuration and create beans

alt Configuration or bean initialization fails
  Context --> Spring : typed startup exception
  Spring -> Lifecycle : ApplicationFailedEvent
  Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.failed\nstage, code, component, root cause
  Spring --> Operator : non-zero process exit
else Context initialization succeeds
  Context -> Gate : after all regular singletons
  Gate -> Logs : startup.check.started database
  Gate -> Database : connect

  alt Database connection fails
      Database --> Gate : SQL or pool exception
      Gate -> Logs : startup.check.completed failure\nfailureStage=startup_database_connect
      Gate --> Spring : required check exception
      Spring -> Lifecycle : ApplicationFailedEvent
      Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.failed\nerrorCode=DATABASE_CONNECT_FAILED
      Spring --> Operator : non-zero process exit
  else Database connects
      Gate -> Database : fixed read-only Session schema probes
    alt Schema or SELECT privilege is invalid
        Database --> Gate : SQL exception
        Gate -> Logs : startup.check.completed failure\nfailureStage=startup_database_schema
        Gate --> Spring : required check exception
        Spring -> Lifecycle : ApplicationFailedEvent
        Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.failed\nerrorCode=DATABASE_SCHEMA_INVALID
        Spring --> Operator : non-zero process exit
    else Session schema is readable
        Gate -> Logs : startup.check.completed success
        Gate -> Logs : startup.check.started agent_cache_root
        Gate -> CacheRoot : safe create, write, and delete probe
      alt Cache root is unavailable
          CacheRoot --> Gate : file-system exception
          Gate -> Logs : startup.check.completed failure\nfailureStage=startup_filesystem
          Gate --> Spring : required check exception
          Spring -> Lifecycle : ApplicationFailedEvent
          Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.failed\nerrorCode=AGENT_CACHE_ROOT_UNAVAILABLE
          Spring --> Operator : non-zero process exit
      else Cache root is writable
          Gate -> Logs : startup.check.completed success
          Gate --> Context : all required checks passed
          Context -> WebServer : start connector and bind port
        alt Web server binding fails
          WebServer --> Spring : port or server exception
          Spring -> Lifecycle : ApplicationFailedEvent
          Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.failed\nfailureStage=startup_web_server
          Spring --> Operator : non-zero process exit
        else Web server binding succeeds
          Spring -> Lifecycle : ApplicationReadyEvent
          Lifecycle -> Logs : startup.completed\noutcome=success
          Spring --> Operator : backend ready
        end
      end
    end
  end
end

note over Lifecycle, Logs
If the logging system cannot initialize, write one sanitized
CAMPUSCLAW_STARTUP_FAILED summary to stderr and keep non-zero exit.
end note

note over Gate, CacheRoot
Remote model, tool, and CampusMate services are not probed here.
They remain lazy runtime dependencies until an approved health API exists.
end note
@enduml

@startuml campusclaw_log_context_propagation
title Diagnostic Context Propagation

' Source evidence:
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/Agent.java:57-58 and 255-278, virtual-thread execution
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/SimpleStreamOptions.java:32-44, current invocation options
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionContextFactory.java:53-65, execution context creation
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeActiveExecution.java:21-59, active execution state
' Observed behavior: request identity is not captured, SimpleStreamOptions.sessionId is not populated by Runtime Agent assembly, and MDC does not cross all asynchronous boundaries by construction.
' Architecture change: create a log-only immutable context, enrich it after persistence, and pass a safe AI diagnostic projection through stream options.
' Design reason: explicit immutable data avoids thread-local loss and prevents credentials or request bodies from entering logging context.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ClassBorderColor #475569
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

class "HttpRequestLogContext" as HttpContext {
  requestId
  parentRequestId
  operation
  method
  routeTemplate
  startNanos
}

class "RuntimeInvocationLogContext" as RuntimeContext {
  requestId
  operation
  sessionId
  agentId
  userEntryId
  modelId
  startNanos
}

class "AiDiagnosticContext" as AiContext {
  requestId
  sessionId
  userEntryId
}

class "ModelInvocationContext" as ModelContext {
  modelInvocationId
  providerId
  modelId
  attempt
  startNanos
}

class "RuntimeActiveExecution" as ActiveExecution
class "SimpleStreamOptions" as StreamOptions
class "MateServiceModelManagerProvider" as Provider
class "RuntimeExecutionCoordinator" as Coordinator
class "Async HTTP Completion State" as AsyncState

HttpContext --> RuntimeContext : enrich after session lookup and user-entry commit
RuntimeContext *-- ActiveExecution : explicit immutable field
RuntimeContext --> AiContext : safe projection only
AiContext *-- StreamOptions : diagnostic field, never serialized upstream
StreamOptions --> Provider
Provider --> ModelContext : create per model attempt
ModelContext --> Provider : exactly one terminal log
RuntimeContext --> Coordinator : execution terminal log
HttpContext *-- AsyncState : exactly one HTTP or SSE completion log

note right of HttpContext
Servlet MDC may mirror requestId while the request thread is active.
It is cleared in finally and never used as async source of truth.
end note

note right of AiContext
No caller headers, credentials, prompt text,
tool arguments, thinking, or response model.
end note

note bottom of AsyncState
Atomic terminal state prevents duplicate logs from
onCompletion, onTimeout, onError, and write failure races.
end note
@enduml
